  "verdict_sentence": "Capacity does bind on 1h (43 max_open_positions rejects vs 453 taken BUYs), but the names we could not buy were worse on mean hold-return at every horizon than the names we did buy. The one Phase-2 stagnant_rotation fire did not reproduce on a clean re-run of the same tight knobs, so there is no redeploy event to score.",
  "verdict": "Capacity binds often enough on 1h to talk about, and the evidence that freed slots would have caught something better is not there.\n\n1. Production max_open=36 binds intermittently (43 denies, 19 days, 19 symbols). Illiquidity (1773) and cash-floor (142) deny more BUYs than slots. 4h never binds.\n2. Mean 24h/72h/7d hold-return of rejected candidates is worse than taken BUYs by 3.59 / 7.58 / 5.32 pp. Medians are mixed (rejected less-bad at 72h/7d) because taken names have a winner tail.\n3. Part B is too thin: the Phase-2 n=1 fire did not reproduce (0 fires, 218 capacity rejects on the tight book). Cannot score redeploy quality.\n\nDo not flip stagnant_rotation_enabled or correlated_tier.enabled in config.json."
